      "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
      "body": "Automated review (high effort): 10 findings, posted inline. The first four mean that seeding does not work end to end yet.\n\n1. A non-dry-run `repo-memory seed` fails on the first batch. I reproduced this locally: it fails with `add: dossier_scope is required`.\n2. Seeded entries would have no type, so they would not render.\n3. Template text from inside code fences gets seeded as real decisions.\n4. `--before` skips every workorder.\n\nThe \"199 entries\" result comes from `--dry-run`, which bypasses op validation.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-06T16:52:35Z",
      "includesCreatedEdit": false,
      "reactionGroups": [],
      "state": "COMMENTED",
      "commit": {
        "oid": "f725dc452c0c1ac26bc0c22aab251e5cbd66df2b"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "PRR_kwDOU197yM8AAAABQ8lwQg",
      "author": {
        "login": "matthewmcneill"
      },
      "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
      "body": "Re-review of 9c53ae7: the fix commit resolves most of the previous findings. Build, vet and the touched package tests pass. A real seed now writes 198 entries and a second run adds none.\n\n**Resolved:** the empty-scope write failure, the `type` vs `entry_type` key, `--before` paths, scope and type on hand-edit add ops, supersede keeping anchors and evidence, a single-transaction rebuild, and the orphaned triage and publish code.\n\n**Still open or newly exposed (inline):** I ran the seed into a scratch dir, and the seeded output has two serious problems.\n- Dossier scopes are being made from prose sentences.\n- 24 entries go to scope `path/to`, and template placeholder text is still seeded.\n\nThe projector's stale-scope handling also still breaks after a move. Seed IDs depend on the absolute path. `ProjectBefore` was removed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-06T17:29:01Z",
      "includesCreatedEdit": false,
      "reactionGroups": [],
      "state": "COMMENTED",
      "commit": {
        "oid": "9c53ae7ae6ec2fda14498f16598430e6a29e4d59"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "PRR_kwDOU197yM8AAAABQ8xdLA",
      "author": {
        "login": "matthewmcneill"
      },
      "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
      "body": "Round-3 re-review of c8282fb. All 9 round-2 items are addressed. Build, vet and tests pass. A real seed writes 174 entries from 49 workorders, a rerun adds none, and no template text or `path/to` scopes remain. The projector now prefers `entryIndex`, `ProjectBefore` is back, and projection runs outside the write transaction.\n\n**The remaining issue is scope quality.** In a real seed run, **95 of 174 entries (55%)** land in PR-name scopes such as `pr-02a-transcript-episode`, and 5 land in `**\\`internal/core/config`. The cause is that change bullets written as prose are now *dropped* instead of having their path extracted. The other inline comments are smaller: the IDs depend on how `--pa-dir` is spelled (verified), seed timestamps, and a few cleanups.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-06T17:45:26Z",
      "includesCreatedEdit": false,
      "reactionGroups": [],
      "state": "COMMENTED",
      "commit": {
        "oid": "c8282fb21150668d4eb30b8a7dc18df3490c44be"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "PRR_kwDOU197yM8AAAABQ89uRg",
      "author": {
        "login": "matthewmcneill"
      },
      "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
      "body": "Round-4 re-review of 3ef424a. Good progress: build, vet and tests pass. A real seed writes 174 entries from 49 workorders, a rerun adds none, scopes are mostly module-based now, op timestamps span Oct 1–6, and ScanAndParse runs once.\n\n**Remaining (inline), three of them reproduced:**\n1. **The time-cut still doesn't work.** Op timestamps are fixed, but batch `created_at` (what `IterateBefore` filters on) is still `time.Now()`.\n2. **Running from a subdirectory regressed.** Paths are now made absolute against the cwd, so `cd internal && repo-memory seed` silently seeds 0 entries.\n3. **About 23% of anchors aren't repo paths** (Go symbols, `~/.gemini/…`, `<data-dir>/…`), and they produce dossier scopes like `~/.gemini/antigravity` and `modernc.org`.\n\nThe others: re-adding an entry under a new scope doesn't actually move it, `--before` uses HEAD's commit time, and a small regex cleanup.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
